      "findingMessages": {
        "schema-gain-max-deviation-key-not-camelcase": "`#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]` on an enum renames only the variant names, not the fields inside struct variants. The JSON key is therefore `max_deviation`, while every other manifest key is camelCase, and the docs (line 34) and the validator error (`gain.maxDeviation`) say `maxDeviation`. A third-party denoise-model.json written as documented, `{\"kind\":\"matchMean\",\"nominal\":1e6,\"maxDeviation\":0.05}`, fails manifest::parse with 'missing field max_deviation', so the model cannot be installed.",
        "schema-manifest-tile-exceeds-remote-limit": "Manifest validation accepts tiles up to 2048 cells, but the remote denoise protocol caps tiles at MAX_TILE = 1024, and serve() refuses to start beyond that. A valid model with tile 1536 installs and runs locally, but `lightcraft-cli denoise-serve` fails with 'tile size 1536 is outside 1..=1024', so its remote denoise can never be used. The two contracts disagree on the accepted range."
      },
      "findingTitles": {
        "schema-gain-max-deviation-key-not-camelcase": "Add `rename_all_fields = \"camelCase\"` to the enum (or `#[serde(rename = \"maxDeviation\", alias = \"max_deviation\")]` on the field) so that existing installed manifests still read.",
        "schema-manifest-tile-exceeds-remote-limit": "Use one shared tile limit: either cap manifest tiles at the remote/GPU limit (1024) or raise remote::MAX_TILE (and its payload bounds) to the manifest's 2048."
      },
